## while loop
just like other programing language, c# has while and for loop either
syntax belike:
```C#
while(condition){

}
```

## do-while loop
the syntax of do-while loop is like:
```C#
do{
    statement;
}
while(condition)
```
From the skeleton, it's easy to understand what the do statement does in the do-while loop.
When the code block is executed, it will run the statement first, then check the condition of while to determine whether continues the loop or not.

## for loop
the syntax belike:
```C#
for(initialization; condition; incrementation/decrementation){
    statement;
}
```

## for-each loop
the for loop has another style, the for-each loop.
the syntax looks like:
```C#
foreach(type variableName in arrayName){
    statement;
}
```
the for-each loop is usually used for iterating something like array.
here is an example:
```C#
string[] cars = {"A", "B", "C"};
foreach(string i in cars){
    Console.WriteLine(i);
} //it will iterate all the elements of the array cars
```
